// Source-owned compiler query orchestration.
// The check query follows the Driver's normal load, declaration-comptime,
// body-comptime, and semantic-finalization phases before serialization.
//
// Incremental service packet design (review contract; no service is installed
// by this comment). Source of truth: Rust QueryService::CompilerQueries and
// CmdTry::verdict. NativeLead selects their invocation-memory mechanism, not
// DriverRecordStore serialization or a second persistent cache.
//
// Ownership and lifetime:
// - One Driver session belongs to one try invocation and survives its edits.
//   It owns document inputs, checked-root memos, the exact external-input
//   closure, volatile-root marks, and one opaque Sema session per root.
// - Checked results are immutable owned packets shared by memo and caller;
//   a hit must not copy the checked graph or execute its body checker again.
// - Sema owns all typed body products and their replay. Driver never opens
//   Sema-private fields. Closing the invocation releases inputs, root memos
//   and every Sema session; no state leaks into a later try invocation.
//
// Authorized input adapter:
// - The CLI retains Request.prepare_overlays as the one filesystem/authority
//   resolver. check_disk prepares the entry without edits; set_document updates
//   the session's exact canonical-path text; check_text prepares the complete
//   overlay set through the same adapter and enters this existing check flow.
// - Driver receives the actual prepared snapshot and parsed entry packet;
//   it does not reopen display paths, infer a project root, or forward to Rust.
// - Roots/modes are distinct query keys. Root text, loaded dependency text,
//   package/lock files, actual external/comptime inputs and every semantic
//   request input participate in freshness. Stamps only avoid re-reading when
//   the authorized adapter proves identity; a stamp never decides freshness.
// - A missing read invalidates the root query and uses the ordinary diagnostic
//   path. Comptime/volatile roots force a root recompute before each verdict.
//   Dependencies discovered by the real check replace the root's closure;
//   failed checks preserve prior dependencies instead of losing invalidation.
//
// Root query flow:
// - Refresh inputs before lookup. An unchanged nonvolatile root returns its
//   immutable checked memo without registration, body checking or fake item
//   hits. Otherwise run the normal load/declaration-comptime/body-comptime/
//   semantic-finalization flow below with the root's opaque Sema session.
// - Keep registration, policies, plugin interfaces, resolved imports and
//   target/profile facts canonical. This is not a BuildGraph/receipt facade,
//   a second frontend, or two complete checks with inferred reuse counters.
//
// Opaque Sema contract (sole implementation editor: SpeedPareto2):
// - Begin-bundle compares the canonical global environment (excluding only
//   BuildStamp.At), span-stripped module interfaces with callable bodies
//   removed, and resolved-import dependencies. Invalidate the changed module
//   interface and its reverse-import closure; a private body edit does not
//   dirty unrelated interfaces. Deleted modules and changed import resolution
//   invalidate their owned entries too.
// - Body inputs include the complete raw function AST, all source spans,
//   raw-protocol-return mode and every checking input. Text-only or span-free
//   fingerprints cannot stand in for this input. Sema supplies this contract;
//   Driver cannot invent a partial serialization of its private state.
// - An entry owns the accepted final typed body and ALL ordered diagnostics,
//   calls, comptime requests, name facts, wanted hooks and checked function
//   facts: completion, exact-Int reachability, copies, hardware use, body
//   sources, compute/failure facts and every pending/publication/summary row.
// - Commit only after the main callback retry accepts the final owned packet
//   with wanted_hooks=false. Never cache a provisional/withheld packet or a
//   partially borrowed parallel worker result. Comptime/embed inputs and a
//   missing/incomplete owned body follow the real recompute path.
// - Replay through the SAME ordered append path used by fresh bodies
//   (currently sema_append_function plus its explicit facts loops), preserving
//   parallel result order. Factoring that path belongs to the checker owner;
//   planned helper names are not existing APIs. Re-run all global failure,
//   effect, borrow and other bundle obligations after all body products join.
//
// Counters and command cutover:
// - Root hits/recomputes and body hits/recomputes are distinct cumulative
//   observations. Increment a body hit only for an actual accepted replay;
//   increment a body recompute once when the tracked initial logical body
//   query accepts its final outcome, including uncached/bypassed outcomes.
//   Provisional callback attempts do not publish or increment separately;
//   global rechecks/probes are not initial body-cache hits/recomputes.
//   No result-derived counts or synthetic cached claims.
// - CmdTry takes stats after its baseline check_disk, installs each staged
//   document, calls check_text, and reports saturating deltas of the actual
//   item counters, exactly as Rust CmdTry313-330.
// - Keep uses the existing SourceTransaction/SemanticOps writer after the
//   checked verdict and current-byte comparison. Default speculation writes
//   no source. Failed checks publish the normal diagnostics, not clean claims.
//
// Acceptance packet:
// - Unchanged root memo executes no body checker; changed private body, moved
//   spans, changed signature/import/interface, deleted module, manifest/lock,
//   volatile comptime and dependency edits exercise their exact invalidation.
// - Fresh and replayed packets agree on diagnostics, names, effects, failure,
//   copies, publications and borrow obligations on serial and parallel paths.
// - Exact try human/JSON output, receipt identity and keep/no-keep transaction
//   behavior use real item-counter deltas. Source approval requires the full
//   typed input/replay/caller packet; parser success is not semantic proof.
use jet_sema.sema_output_resolve
use jet_foundation.[
    Diagnostic,
    MIRSourceFile,
    mir_source_file_id,
]
use jet_sema.[
    SemaCompilerModuleSource,
    SemaComptimeFunctionResult,
    SemaComptimeItemValue,
    SemaForeignProviderInput,
    SemaGraphResult,
    SemaRegistrationGraph,
    SemaRegistrationModuleInput,
    SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy,
    sema_collect_comptime_declarations,
    sema_finalize_registration_graph,
    sema_registration_prepare_graph,
]
use jet_eval.[
    JetCompilerServicesCheckedFacts,
    JetCompilerServicesCheckedInput,
    JetCompilerServicesParseFacts,
    jet_eval_compiler_services_checked,
]

pub struct JetDriverCompilerCheckInput {
    pub parsed: JetCompilerServicesParseFacts
    pub request: JetDriverCompileRequest
}

pub struct JetDriverCompilerCheckResult {
    pub checked: JetCompilerServicesCheckedFacts?
    pub diagnostics: [Diagnostic]
    pub failed_stage: JetDriverStage?
    pub complete: Bool
    pub internal_problem: String?
}

fn jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load: JetDriverLoadResult, stage: JetDriverStage, problem: String?) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult Never! {
    JetDriverCompilerCheckResult{checked: None, diagnostics: load.diagnostics, failed_stage: Val(stage), complete: false, internal_problem: problem}
}

fn jet_driver_compiler_check_registration_inputs(load: JetDriverLoadResult, providers: [SemaForeignProviderInput], diagnostics: &[Diagnostic]) -> [SemaRegistrationModuleInput]? {
    inputs := [SemaRegistrationModuleInput]{ }
    source_positions :: jet_driver_source_file_positions(load.source_files)
    loop module_index in 0..<load.modules.len() {
        loaded_module :: load.modules[module_index]
        if loaded_module.source_unit_index < 0 || loaded_module.source_unit_index >= load.source_units.len() {
            &diagnostics.push(jet_driver_diagnostic_without_span("E0003", "a loaded module has no exact source-unit owner", "semantic registration preserves the loader's canonical source-unit identity", "retain the source-unit index returned by JetDriver"))
            return None
        }
        unit := load.source_units[loaded_module.source_unit_index]
        handles :: jet_driver_registration_foreign_handle_facts(loaded_module.module_identity, providers, &diagnostics) ?? return None
        &inputs.push(SemaRegistrationModuleInput{
            package_identity: loaded_module.package_identity,
            module_identity: loaded_module.module_identity,
            module_name: loaded_module.module_name,
            module_path: jet_driver_module_display(unit.relative_path),
            source_file: unit.path,
            source_segments: unit.source_segments,
            source_origin: unit.source_origin,
            program: loaded_module.program,
            foreign_handles: handles,
            source: jet_driver_source_text_at(load.source_files, source_positions, unit.path),
        })
    }
    Val(inputs)
}

fn jet_driver_compiler_check_package_policies(load: JetDriverLoadResult) -> [SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy] Never! {
    policies := [SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy]{ }
    loop package in load.packages {
        &policies.push(SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy{
            package_identity: package.identity,
            authority_allow: package.authority_allow,
            authority_deny: package.authority_deny,
            authority_needs: package.authority_needs,
            runtime_ceiling: package.runtime_ceiling,
            edition: package.edition,
        })
    }
    policies
}
fn jet_driver_compiler_check_source_bytes(load: JetDriverLoadResult, path: String) -> String? {
    found := String?{None}
    loop file in load.source_files {
        if file.path != path -> next
        if found != None -> return None
        found = Val(file.source)
    }
    found
}

// Path -> position of its first loaded source text, built once per compile so
// each module reads its text without rescanning the file list.
fn jet_driver_source_file_positions(files: [MIRSourceFile]) -> [String:Int] Never! {
    positions := [String:Int]{}
    loop (index, file) in files {
        if positions.get(file.path) == None -> positions[file.path] = index
    }
    positions
}

// The loaded text of `path`; a module with no loaded text (a compiler-synthetic
// unit) has none.
fn jet_driver_source_text_at(files: [MIRSourceFile], positions: [String:Int], path: String) -> String Never! {
    if positions.get(path) == .Val(index) -> return files[index].source
    ""
}

fn jet_driver_compiler_check_module_sources(load: JetDriverLoadResult, canonical: SemaRegistrationModuleInput, canonical_source: String, parsed: JetCompilerServicesParseFacts) -> [SemaCompilerModuleSource]? {
    rows := [SemaCompilerModuleSource]{}
    loop loaded_module in load.modules {
        if loaded_module.source_unit_index < 0 || loaded_module.source_unit_index >= load.source_units.len() -> return None
        unit := load.source_units[loaded_module.source_unit_index]
        source := jet_driver_compiler_check_source_bytes(load, unit.path) ?? return None
        if loaded_module.module_identity == load.entry_module_identity {
            if source != parsed.source -> return None
            if parsed.compiler_source.len() > 0 {
                if parsed.compiler_source.len() != source.len() -> return None
                source = parsed.compiler_source
            }
        }
        duplicate := false
        loop existing in rows {
            if existing.module_identity == loaded_module.module_identity -> duplicate = true
        }
        if duplicate -> return None
        &rows.push(SemaCompilerModuleSource{module_identity: loaded_module.module_identity, source: source})
    }
    loop existing in rows {
        if existing.module_identity == canonical.module_identity -> return None
    }
    &rows.push(SemaCompilerModuleSource{module_identity: canonical.module_identity, source: canonical_source})
    Val(rows)
}


fn jet_driver_compiler_check_result(input: JetDriverCompilerCheckInput, registration: ^SemaRegistrationGraph, graph: ^SemaGraphResult, module_sources: [SemaCompilerModuleSource], diagnostics: [Diagnostic]) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult {
    graph_complete :: graph.complete
    checked := jet_eval_compiler_services_checked(JetCompilerServicesCheckedInput{
        parsed: input.parsed,
        registration: ^registration,
        graph: ^graph,
        module_sources: module_sources,
        diagnostics: diagnostics,
    })
    complete := graph_complete && checked.semantic_index_complete
    JetDriverCompilerCheckResult{checked: Val(checked), diagnostics: diagnostics, failed_stage: None, complete: complete, internal_problem: None}
}
fn jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(
    input: JetDriverCompilerCheckInput,
    registration: ^SemaRegistrationGraph,
    graph: ^SemaGraphResult,
    module_sources: [SemaCompilerModuleSource],
    diagnostics: [Diagnostic],
) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult? {
    if graph.modules.len() != registration.modules.len() || !jet_driver_has_errors(diagnostics) -> return None
    Val(jet_driver_compiler_check_result(input, ^registration, ^graph, module_sources, diagnostics))
}

fn jet_driver_compiler_check_parse_only(load: JetDriverLoadResult) -> Bool Never! {
    if load.modules.len() == 0 -> return false
    if load.failed_stage == .Val(stage) -> return stage == JetDriverStage.Parse
    false
}


pub fn jet_driver_compiler_check(input: JetDriverCompilerCheckInput) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult {
    load := jet_driver_load(input.request)
    parse_only := jet_driver_compiler_check_parse_only(load)
    if (!load.complete || jet_driver_has_errors(load.diagnostics)) && !parse_only -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, load.failed_stage ?? JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    canonical_option := jet_driver_canonical_effect_module(input.request.canonical_effect_source)
    if canonical_option == None -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the embedded compiler-owned Prelude effect source is invalid"))
    canonical := canonical_option ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the embedded compiler-owned Prelude effect source is unavailable"))
    loop unit in load.source_units {
        if jet_driver_module_identity(unit.package_identity, unit.relative_path) == canonical.module_identity || unit.path == canonical.source_file {
            return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, Val("an authorized source unit collides with the pinned compiler-owned Prelude effect source"))
        }
    }
    &load.generated_source_files.push(MIRSourceFile{id: mir_source_file_id(canonical.source_file), path: canonical.source_file, source: input.request.canonical_effect_source})
    providers := jet_driver_assemble_foreign_providers(input.request.authorized_sources, &load)
    if (!load.complete || jet_driver_has_errors(load.diagnostics)) && !parse_only -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    if !jet_driver_foreign_provider_owners_valid(load.modules, providers, &load.diagnostics) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    module_sources :: jet_driver_compiler_check_module_sources(load, canonical, input.request.canonical_effect_source, input.parsed) ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the compiler query source is not the exact loaded entry or a loaded module source is missing"))
    target_option := jet_driver_selected_target_machine(input.request, &load.diagnostics)
    if target_option == None -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, None)
    target :: target_option ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, None)
    // The stage callees read `load` while they append diagnostics, so the
    // diagnostics list travels beside it and is put back after each stage.
    stage_diagnostics := load.diagnostics
    load.diagnostics = [Diagnostic]{}
    registration_inputs_option := jet_driver_compiler_check_registration_inputs(load, providers, &stage_diagnostics)
    load.diagnostics = stage_diagnostics
    registration_inputs := registration_inputs_option ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    canonical_identity := canonical.module_identity
    &registration_inputs.push(^canonical)
    loop index in 0..<registration_inputs.len() {
        if registration_inputs[index].module_identity == load.entry_module_identity {
            registration_inputs[index].program = input.parsed.parsed.program
        }
    }
    registration := sema_registration_prepare_graph(
        registration_inputs,
        load.imports,
        load.package_identity,
        load.entry_module_identity,
        canonical_identity,
        providers,
        target,
        jet_driver_build_facts(load, input.request, target),
        false,
    )
    output_diagnostics :: sema_output_resolve(&registration, input.request.output_intent, input.request.output_address)
    loop diagnostic in output_diagnostics -> &registration.diagnostics.push(diagnostic)
    if jet_driver_has_errors(output_diagnostics) -> registration.complete = false
    if registration.internal_problem == .Val(problem) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val(problem))
    stage := sema_collect_comptime_declarations(registration, jet_driver_compiler_check_package_policies(load), input.request.eval_config.host_hooks, input.request.compiler_threads, input.request.trace_sink)
    if !stage.complete || stage.modules.len() != registration_inputs.len() || jet_driver_has_errors(stage.diagnostics) {
        jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(&load.diagnostics, stage.diagnostics)
        if stage.modules.len() == registration_inputs.len() {
            provisional := sema_finalize_registration_graph(registration, None, stage, [SemaComptimeItemValue]{}, [SemaComptimeFunctionResult]{}, input.request.eval_config.host_hooks, input.request.compiler_threads, input.request.trace_sink)
            jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(&load.diagnostics, provisional.diagnostics)
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, ^registration, ^provisional, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        if !jet_driver_has_errors(load.diagnostics) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val(jet_driver_incomplete_graph_problem("semantic declaration checking did not return a complete resolved package graph ({stage.modules.len()} of {registration_inputs.len()} modules checked)", stage.modules)))
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, None)
    }
    initial_values := [SemaComptimeItemValue]{ }
    stage_diagnostics = load.diagnostics
    load.diagnostics = [Diagnostic]{}
    // The declaration pass's graph copy becomes the run's environment graph.
    staged_graph := ^stage.graph
    stage.graph = None
    run := jet_driver_run_comptime(
        registration,
        ^staged_graph,
        stage.sources,
        stage.names,
        initial_values,
        [SemaComptimeFunctionResult]{},
        load,
        input.request,
        &stage_diagnostics,
    )
    load.diagnostics = stage_diagnostics
    if run.soft_stop -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, None)
    if !run.complete {
        if run.internal_problem == None {
            provisional := sema_finalize_registration_graph(registration, None, stage, run.values, run.functions, input.request.eval_config.host_hooks, input.request.compiler_threads, input.request.trace_sink)
            jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(&load.diagnostics, provisional.diagnostics)
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, ^registration, ^provisional, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, run.internal_problem)
    }
    run_graph := ^run.graph
    run.graph = None
    graph := sema_finalize_registration_graph(registration, ^run_graph, stage, run.values, run.functions, input.request.eval_config.host_hooks, input.request.compiler_threads, input.request.trace_sink)
    if graph.modules.len() != registration_inputs.len() {
        jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(&load.diagnostics, graph.diagnostics)
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("semantic finalization did not return every registered module"))
    }
    loop diagnostic in jet_driver_check_schema_migrations(input.request, registration, graph) -> &load.diagnostics.push(diagnostic)
    stage_diagnostics = load.diagnostics
    load.diagnostics = [Diagnostic]{}
    body_run := jet_driver_orchestrate_comptime_bodies(
        registration,
        stage,
        ^graph,
        run.values,
        run.functions,
        jet_driver_empty_compile_trace(),
        load,
        input.request,
        &stage_diagnostics,
    )
    load.diagnostics = stage_diagnostics
    if body_run.soft_stop -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, None)
    if !body_run.complete {
        if body_run.internal_problem == None {
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, ^registration, ^body_run.graph, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, body_run.internal_problem)
    }
    graph = ^body_run.graph
    stage_diagnostics = load.diagnostics
    load.diagnostics = [Diagnostic]{}
    validation := jet_driver_validate_checked_text(
        registration,
        stage,
        ^graph,
        body_run.values,
        body_run.functions,
        body_run.trace,
        load,
        input.request,
        &stage_diagnostics,
    )
    load.diagnostics = stage_diagnostics
    if validation.soft_stop -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, None)
    if !validation.complete {
        if validation.internal_problem == None {
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, ^registration, ^validation.graph, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, validation.internal_problem)
    }
    graph = ^validation.graph
    jet_driver_compiler_check_result(input, ^registration, ^graph, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
}
